# README wording — YOURS. The scaffold creates this file once and never
# overwrites it.
#
# A slot set here words the generated README files over the same slot of
# main.kit.info, where apidef puts the spec's metadata. A slot left out keeps
# the spec's wording. Text edited into a generated README is lost on the next
# generate; text here is not.
#
#   main: kit: text: {
#     tagline: 'Payments, invoices and refunds from TypeScript, Go and Python.'
#     summary: 'Acme Pay is a payments API for marketplaces.'
#     entity_desc: { invoice: 'A bill sent to a customer.' }
#   }
#
# The slots are title, summary, website, tagline, about_md, homepage,
# docs_url, meta_source and entity_desc. Any other key fails the model build.

main: kit: text: {
  summary: 'An unofficial TypeScript and Python client for the [Figma REST API](https://developers.figma.com/docs/rest-api/). It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Figma.'
  about_md: 'The Figma REST API reads and writes Figma files, comments, components, styles, variables, webhooks and more. This SDK is generated from the [OpenAPI spec Figma publishes](https://github.com/figma/rest-api-spec).\n\n## Demo\n\n`demo/feedback.ts` turns a file\'s comments into a checklist. It lists the unresolved comments on the Figma file named by `FIGMA_FILE_KEY`, writes `demo/FEEDBACK.md` grouped by frame with author and date (replies under their parent, resolved comments skipped), and replies "Logged" once to each unresolved thread, so a second run adds nothing. It calls only the comments endpoints; frame names come from a saved file nodes response in `fixtures/file-nodes.json`.\n\nIt needs Node 24 or later, a built `ts/` and a `.env` with `FIGMA_TOKEN` and `FIGMA_FILE_KEY`:\n\n```sh\n(cd ts && npm install && npm run build)\nnode demo/feedback.ts                      # list comments, write FEEDBACK.md, reply\nnode demo/feedback.ts --fetch-frame-names  # also refresh frame names: one GET file nodes call\nnode --test "demo/*.test.ts"               # offline test against fixtures/\n```'
}
